        // We can't directly inherit from the `leftarm`/`rightarm` bones (or even set the `binding` property to them, absent a pivot), because it causes the hardcoded `v.short_arm_offset_left`/`v.short_arm_offset_right` variables to always return 0.
        // The workaround I came up with for this is really nasty: duplicate all `leftarm`/`rightarm` transformations in 3rd person to the `leftarm_custom`/`rightarm_custom` bones so it propagates to the armor model.
        // Additionally, because emote transformations are hardcoded, we can't actually apply the hurt armor model while emoting because we can't duplicate bone transformations applied by emotes.
